														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4629643">
									

<p>Hello hello!</p>
<p>I’m Kara from the Site Crit team!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Ze&nbsp;Crit&nbsp;O’&nbsp;Doom</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>- “To date, only one episode of SCP-5123 has ever been seen” Huh? This is a little confusing when paired with the statement after that “with variations ranging from slight dialogue changes to altered guests and sequences occurring upon each subsequent airing.” Is this trying to suggest that this is a re-run that is changing every time it airs?</p>
<p>- “the show will end and be replaced by the channel's usual scheduling.” So what you’re saying is that this airing just cuts into the programming that was previously scheduled? Did people notice this before the Foundation stepped in?</p>
<p>- “Carter:Too bad you couldn't get a job as a paper reader, huh?” There needs to be a space between the colon. Along that vein “SCP-5123-1: No, not as funny as that.It felt like a natural ending to my career, I suppose.” There should be a space between the period and 'It'.</p>
<p>Final notes:</p>
<p>This SCP is quite interesting, but I’m a little confused by the ending. What did he do? Kill the original -1 who dared to go against him? That part felt a little foggy to me and I couldn’t exactly understand what you were trying to get at beyond the kidnapping of people and making them play these characters. It’s a great story, but it feels like a little more clarity would be useful.</p>
<p>Great job on this, and I hope to see more from you in the future.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
