<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The video log is (<em>almost</em> entirely) on-point.</p>
<p>The dialogue is fine, though -1's complete breakdown personally comes off as a little too on-the-nose<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-126168-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-126168-1')">1</a></sup> and a touch on the narmy side.</p>
<p>There are a few minor details in the log that I think contribute very well to giving this a little extra flavor (audience members wiping their eyes/weird stain/a novel type of Eye Scream/Dave) and overall I think there's a version of this that could make a lasting impression.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>My primary issue with this is that it spends several paragraphs very thoroughly describing what is essentially the entire plot without nuance regarding its trajectory. The (more effective) video doesn't grow or progress from this point; it simply showcases it.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-126168-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-126168-1')">1</a>. Doubly so with the footnote - that their identity can be verified does nothing but belabor the point.</div>
</div>

